# Build-context hygiene. Deliberately conservative: only things that are never needed at build
# time are excluded, because a file ignored here silently breaks whichever stage COPYs it. The
# context that remains (source, docs, tests, tools, governance markdown, workflows) is a few
# hundred kilobytes, and each stage chooses exactly what it copies.
.git
.gitignore
.venv
.env
.env.*
node_modules
npm-debug.log*
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
build/
dist/
*.egg-info
*.marked.txt
requirements-audit.txt
requirements.sbom.txt
release-notes.md
*.log
.DS_Store

# The documentation *sources* are needed by the docs stage. The generated site under build/ is
# not: it is rebuilt inside the image, so an image can never ship docs that drifted from its code.
